  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "💃 Girl Group Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for a girl group with harmonies, attitude and a dance routine."
    },
    "intro": "Good girl group names sound fun, bold and a little bit cheeky: a \"Girls\" name, a sparkly plural or one confident word. This **girl group name generator** makes group names, member names and album titles in the patterns the great pop girl groups used.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good girl group names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator, with members and an album:</p><ul><li><strong>Rebel Belles</strong>: attitude and a rhyme, two things girl groups do well.</li><li><strong>Girls in Charge</strong>: the \"Girls\" name with a statement attached.</li><li><strong>Sunset Sisters</strong>: a sisters name, whether or not they're related.</li><li><strong>The Hi-Fis</strong>: a 60s-style plural with \"The\" in front.</li><li><strong>Mirrorball</strong>: one shiny word, made for a disco-pop group.</li><li><strong>Ruby Devlin</strong>: a member name with a bit of sparkle.</li><li><strong>Ivy Thorne</strong>: a member name for the one with attitude.</li><li><strong>Rewrite the Ending</strong>: an album title that sounds like a comeback.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "How girl groups get their names",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>The 60s plural.</strong> The Supremes, the Ronettes and the Shangri-Las set the pattern: \"The\" and a plural. The generator makes names like <em>The Hi-Fis</em>.</li><li><strong>Girls names.</strong> Spice Girls and Girls Aloud put the word in the name. Here: <em>Girls Unstoppable</em>, <em>Girls in Gold</em>.</li><li><strong>Initials and wordplay.</strong> TLC took its name from the initials of T-Boz, Left Eye and Chilli. Wordplay names here include <em>G-Lamour</em> and <em>Glam-Ur</em>.</li><li><strong>Nicknames.</strong> Each of the Spice Girls was given a nickname by the press: Scary, Sporty, Baby, Ginger and Posh. It's worth giving your members one too.</li></ul><p>Girls Aloud were formed on the television show <em>Popstars: The Rivals</em> in 2002, and Little Mix were the first group to win <em>The X Factor</em>, in 2011. Choose <strong>Member name</strong> for a line-up and <strong>Album</strong> for titles like <em>Sisters First</em> or <em>Velvet Days</em>.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Using the names",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>For a story, a show or a hen party act,</strong> give each member a nickname as well as a name.</li><li><strong>For a real group</strong>, check the name on Spotify, YouTube and social media, and make sure it isn't trademarked.</li></ul><p>For a matching boy band, try the <a href=\"boy-band-name-generator.html\">Boy Band Name Generator</a>. For K-pop, there's the <a href=\"kpop-name-generator.html\">K-pop Name Generator</a>, and for a solo star the <a href=\"pop-star-name-generator.html\">Pop Star Name Generator</a>.</p><p>For more genres, see all the <a href=\"../categories/music_genres-names.html\">music genre name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What are good girl group names?",
        "answer": "Fun, bold names: a \"Girls\" name like Girls in Charge, a sparkly plural like Rebel Belles, or one confident word like Mirrorball. The best ones are easy to chant and say something about the group's attitude."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I get names for each member?",
        "answer": "Yes. Choose Member name for a first name and surname, like Ruby Devlin or Ivy Thorne. Give each member a nickname too, the way the Spice Girls had theirs."
      },
      {
        "question": "Are these real girl groups?",
        "answer": "No, they're made up. A few common words may match an existing act, so search the name before using it for a real group."
      }
    ]
